<title>JAPAN: U.S. Treasury market closed in Tokyo for holiday.</title>
<headline>U.S. Treasury market closed in Tokyo for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury market is closed in Tokyo on Monday for the Veteran's Day holiday in the United States.</p>
<p>The market will resume trading on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, Treasury prices ended lower in New York in a shortened session, with the new 6-1/2 percent benchmark 30-year bond standing at 99-29/32, down 10/32 to yield 6.51 percent.</p>
</text>
